          "number": 6,
          "letter": "F",
          "english": "Marconi invented the idea of global communication—or, more straightforwardly, globally networked, mobile, wireless communication. Initially, this was wireless Morse code telegraphy(电报通讯), the principal communication technology of his day. Marconi was the first to develop a practical method for wireless telegraphy using radio waves. He borrowed technical details from many sources, but what set him apart was a self-confident vision of the power of communication technology on the one hand, and, on the other, of the steps that needed to be taken to consolidate his own position as a player in that field. Tracing Marconi's lifeline leads us into the story of modern communication itself. There were other important figures, but Marconi towered over them all in reach, power, and influence, as well as in the grip he had on the popular imagination of his time. Marconi was quite simply the central figure in the emergence of a modern understanding of communication.",
          "chinese": "马可尼构想出了全球通信，或者更直白地说，全球联网、移动的无线通信。最初，这种通信是无线莫尔斯电码电报通信，即他那个时代的主要通信技术。马可尼是第一个利用无线电波开发出实用无线电报方法的人。他从许多来源借鉴了技术细节，但使他与众不同的是：一方面，他自信地看到了通信技术的力量；另一方面，他也清楚地认识到，为了巩固自己作为这一领域参与者的地位，需要采取哪些步骤。追溯马可尼的人生轨迹，就是走进现代通信本身的历史。还有其他重要人物，但无论在影响范围、力量和影响力方面，还是在他对当时大众想象力的掌控方面，马可尼都远远超过了他们。马可尼简直就是现代通信观念兴起过程中的核心人物。",
